Q: How to disable minify in webpack 4 succesfully? A: <p>You can use the <code>terser-webpack-plugin</code> and change configurations to preserve the original variable/function names.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const TerserPlugin = require('terser-webpack-plugin');

module.exports = {
  optimization: {
    minimizer: [
      new TerserPlugin({
        parallel: true,
        terserOptions: {
          // https://github.com/webpack-contrib/terser-webpack-plugin#terseroptions
        },
      }),
    ],
  },
};
</code></pre>

Q: Why is the terminal outputting &quot;0&quot; in this code? A: <p>Your loop depends on the <em>variable</em> <code>fibonnaci</code> to be an even number so it can increment <code>sum</code>, but <code>fibonnaci</code> is initialized as <code>3</code> and never gets changed, so <code>sum</code> is never incremented.</p>
<p>A proper fibonacci <em>function</em> using recursion, just like it is defined in <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibonacci_sequence" rel="nofollow noreferrer">math</a>, can be written as follows:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;

long long fibonacci(long long n) {
    return (n &lt;= 1) ? n : fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}

int main() {
    long long n = 10; // or any positive number
    std::cout &lt;&lt; fibonacci(n) &lt;&lt; std::endl;
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Gmail Filter Export xml file schema not supported? A: <blockquote>
<p><em>retrieve the rule text in the apps:property name=&quot;hasTheWord&quot; field</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>You can do that without a schema by working with the text directly, like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function getField_(xml, field) {
  const regex = new RegExp(`name=&quot;${field}&quot;\s*value=&quot;([^&quot;]+)`);
  return String(xml).match(regex)?.[1];
}

function test() {
  const xml = '&lt;feed xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom&quot; xmlns:apps=&quot;http://schemas.google.com/apps/2006&quot;&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Mail Filters&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;id&gt;tag:mail.google.com&lt;/id&gt;
  &lt;updated&gt;2026-08-26T12:46:36Z&lt;/updated&gt;
  &lt;author&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;MyName&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;email&gt;myemail@gmail.com&lt;/email&gt;
  &lt;/author&gt;
  &lt;entry&gt;
    &lt;category term=&quot;filter&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;Mail Filter&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;id&gt;tag:mail.google.com,2008:filter:z0000001636162795628*2690246542330417407&lt;/id&gt;
    &lt;updated&gt;2026-08-26T12:46:36Z&lt;/updated&gt;
    &lt;content/&gt;
    &lt;apps:property name=&quot;hasTheWord&quot; value=&quot;from:smith OR subject:webinar&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;apps:property name=&quot;shouldArchive&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;apps:property name=&quot;shouldNeverSpam&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;apps:property name=&quot;sizeOperator&quot; value=&quot;s_sl&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;apps:property name=&quot;sizeUnit&quot; value=&quot;s_smb&quot;/&gt;
  &lt;/entry&gt;';
  console.log(getField_(xml, 'hasTheWord'));
}
</code></pre>
<p>Note that the <code>getField_()</code> function will only get the first match, or <code>undefined</code> if there are no matches.</p>
<p>See <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/match" rel="nofollow noreferrer">String.match()</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Optional_chaining" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Optional chaining</a>.</p>
